-- pairs1h-v11.sql  -  the morning check of the MACD fade e-mails on the 1-hour chart for the THREE PAIRS that stay on it (EUR/JPY, AUD/JPY, EUR/USD), rule v11.
-- ONE read-only statement (WITH ... SELECT) for mcp__Supabase__execute_sql. Replace the two markers START_MS and END_MS (each written once, in double curly braces, in the first CTE) by the epoch
-- milliseconds of the range: bars are judged by their OPEN time, START_MS <= open < END_MS; the Routine's day is (X-2d) 21:00 UTC .. (X-1d) 21:00 UTC,
-- END_MS = START_MS + 86400000. Nothing else is to be edited.
-- It is pairs-v11.sql (README.md v11) with a three-row syms (syms-pairs1h-v11.part) and this header, and nothing else: the same parts (head, front-pairs-v9, the engine,
-- back1-v11, guard-pairs, dayend-pairs-v4, back2-v11), the same rule id macdx_12_26_9_w600_1h_fade96of120_in_v11, the same go-live constant (1795003200000, set at v40's
-- release, README.md v11.1); its RUN row says pairs1h.sql v11. Every CTE is scoped by syms, so each SUMMARY and LINE of the three pairs is pairs-v11's.
-- Why (research/macdfade15min-prod-spec.md 7.3, the per-pair form): signal-alerts v41 moves USD/JPY and AUD/USD to the 15-minute chart (pairs-v12.sql) and keeps EUR/JPY,
-- AUD/JPY and EUR/USD on v40's form, the same id and the same '1h' rows. pairs-v11.sql holds all five pairs: run after the switch day, its USD/JPY and AUD/USD rows would be
-- missing at every 1-hour entry (its statements have a start and no end) and, once their '1h' subscriptions are deleted, no_subscription. So from the GMO day after the
-- switch day this statement is sent in place of pairs-v11.sql (README.md v12.1); pairs-v11.sql stays for the switch day and a rollback.
-- It recounts the rule (signal-alerts v40 and v41 for these three, research/macdfade1h-prod-spec.md: at a closed 1-HOUR bar, the MACD line, the blue line, is at 96% of the
-- top / bottom edge of the MACD pane of the newest 120 bars and was not one bar earlier in the same 600-bar window; the FADE side: top -> SELL, bottom -> BUY; the price in is
-- the bar's ask close on a BUY and bid close on a SELL; no stop and no target) from public.gmo_kline_files (interval 1hour) as production reads the data, and compares the
-- expected entries with public.signal_alerts (kind signal, interval 1h, that rule id): the bar, the side, the entry against the ask / bid close, one side a bar
-- (other_side), no stop or target (stop_or_target).
-- It reads no user_id / event_id / e-mail address and writes nothing.
-- Result: columns row_type (RUN | SUMMARY | LINE), instrument, bar_open_utc, side, verdict, data (json). See README.md (sections v12, v11 and v8) for every field.
-- Written to be run in well under a minute (one day: about 1 second).
